# kex: check-only
# A module's last segment names it only where a `using` loads it (or in the
# prelude). With no `using Data.Set` the walker has no `UnorderedSet`
# (`undefined function: UnorderedSet.from`) and BEAM no module to call
# (`undef`), so the checker must not guess `Data.UnorderedSet` either
# (kexhq/kex#840): it names the module that has it instead.
main do
  IO.printLine(UnorderedSet.from([1, 2, 2]).count.to(String))
  IO.printLine(Headers.empty.inspected)
end
